Sample libraries can be rebuilt using TensileCreateLibrary.

SolutionLibraries:
../Tensile/bin/TensileCreateLibrary  --library-format=yaml --no-lazy-library-loading ${HIPBLASLT_DIR}/tensilelite/tests/configs/mixed_configs/ . HIP
../Tensile/bin/TensileCreateLibrary  --library-format=msgpack --no-lazy-library-loading ${HIPBLASLT_DIR}/tensilelite/tests/configs/mixed_configs/ . HIP

KernelsLite.dat is a small (9-solution) master library used by
IndexedLibraryLoad_test, which converts it to the indexed (format_version 2)
layout in process and checks the two loads agree. Any small master library works
here; the only requirement is that it carries every field the current
serialization marks required, so it needs regenerating with the msgpack command
above whenever a required field is added. A fixture that has fallen behind makes
those tests skip with a message rather than fail.

All libraries are checked in as .gz to reduce checkout size
